# Line-ending and binary handling.
#
# Text files are stored and checked out with LF on every platform, so a
# Windows clone (core.autocrlf=true) matches the Linux CI build byte for byte.
# Binary assets are never converted or diffed as text; without this, Git's
# content heuristic can treat a PDF as text and rewrite its line endings.
#
# Rules are explicit per extension on purpose (no "* text=auto"), so a file
# type that is not listed keeps Git's default behavior.

# Text
*.ts          text eol=lf
*.js          text eol=lf
*.css         text eol=lf
*.html        text eol=lf
*.json        text eol=lf
*.md          text eol=lf
*.txt         text eol=lf
*.yml         text eol=lf
*.yaml        text eol=lf
.gitignore    text eol=lf
.gitattributes text eol=lf

# Binary
*.pdf         binary
*.png         binary
*.jpg         binary
*.jpeg        binary
*.webp        binary
*.gif         binary
*.ico         binary
*.mp4         binary
*.woff2       binary
